From 90fe8ff0c2478e42391d807753fda6037913a5ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 23:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] interconnect: qcom: msm8998: compensate BIMC AB votes like downstream

The downstream bus driver derates the BIMC fabric by a 153% utilisation
factor (msm8998-bus.dtsi, fab-bimc qcom,util-fact = <153>), so a
consumer's average-bandwidth request is served with 1.53x headroom.
Apply the same coefficient through ab_coeff, as msm8953 and sdm660
already do, so AB-heavy consumers (display scanout) get the DDR
frequency downstream would have given them.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/interconnect/qcom/msm8998.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/msm8998.c b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/msm8998.c
index c5f4a02..9bc0a0a 100644
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/msm8998.c
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/msm8998.c
@@ -1436,6 +1436,7 @@ static const struct qcom_icc_desc msm8998_bimc = {
 	.num_nodes = ARRAY_SIZE(msm8998_bimc_nodes),
 	.bus_clk_desc = &bimc_clk,
 	.keep_alive = true,
+	.ab_coeff = 153,
 };
 
 static struct qcom_icc_node * const msm8998_cnoc_nodes[] = {
-- 
2.55.0

